    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 397.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.44,
      "text": "We'll cover bundler setup in a future"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 399.84,
      "durationSeconds": 4.6,
      "text": "video. Let's talk about which files"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 402.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.36,
      "text": "TypeScript even looks at."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 404.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.28,
      "text": "The include array tells the compiler"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 406.6,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "where to find your source, usually"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 408.72,
      "durationSeconds": 5.68,
      "text": "everything inside src."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 411.16,
      "durationSeconds": 5.96,
      "text": "The exclude array tells it what to skip."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 414.4,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "You almost always exclude node modules"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 417.12,
      "durationSeconds": 4.44,
      "text": "and your output dist folder, because"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 419.28,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "compiling those would be slow and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 421.56,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "pointless."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 422.96,
      "durationSeconds": 4.12,
      "text": "A common beginner mistake is forgetting"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 425.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "include entirely,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 427.08,
      "durationSeconds": 5.24,
      "text": "which makes TypeScript scan your whole"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 429.24,
      "durationSeconds": 5.8,
      "text": "project and slow to a crawl. Two more"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 432.32,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "options that make life easier."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 435.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Source map generates a map file that"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 437.36,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "links your compiled JavaScript back to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 439.68,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "your original TypeScript. So, when you"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 442.08,
      "durationSeconds": 6.04,
      "text": "debug, you see your real source code,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 444.72,
      "durationSeconds": 7.56,
      "text": "not the messy compiled output."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 448.12,
      "durationSeconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Declaration generates dot d.ts files,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 452.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.12,
      "text": "which are type definition files."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 454.6,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "You only need declaration if you're"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 456.4,
      "durationSeconds": 3.24,
      "text": "publishing a library that others will"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 458.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.08,
      "text": "import."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 459.64,
      "durationSeconds": 5.12,
      "text": "For a regular app, skip it. Let me give"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 462.52,
      "durationSeconds": 4.04,
      "text": "you a few modern flags worth turning on"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 464.76,
      "durationSeconds": 4.44,
      "text": "in 2026."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 466.56,
      "durationSeconds": 5.36,
      "text": "ES module interrupt makes importing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 469.2,
      "durationSeconds": 5.2,
      "text": "common JS packages painless."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 471.92,
      "durationSeconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Skip lib check speeds up compilation by"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 474.4,
      "durationSeconds": 6.6,
      "text": "skipping type checks on library files."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 477.52,
      "durationSeconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Force consistent casing in file names"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 481,
      "durationSeconds": 4.6,
      "text": "prevents headaches when your code works"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 483.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "on Mac, but breaks on a Linux server"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 485.6,
      "durationSeconds": 5.32,
      "text": "because of capital letters."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 487.72,
      "durationSeconds": 5.56,
      "text": "And verbatim module syntax is the modern"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 490.92,
      "durationSeconds": 4.48,
      "text": "way to keep your import and export"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 493.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "handling predictable."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 495.4,
      "durationSeconds": 4.92,
      "text": "These are all safe defaults. Here's a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 497.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.76,
      "text": "complete production-ready tsconfig you"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 500.32,
      "durationSeconds": 3.44,
      "text": "can actually use today."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 502.2,
      "durationSeconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Strict mode on,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 503.76,
      "durationSeconds": 4.04,
      "text": "modern target and module,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 505.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.119,
      "text": "clean path aliases,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 507.8,
      "durationSeconds": 5.44,
      "text": "source maps for debugging,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 509.919,
      "durationSeconds": 5.961,
      "text": "and proper include and exclude."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 513.24,
      "durationSeconds": 5,
      "text": "Copy this, tweak the paths to match your"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 515.88,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "folders, and you've got a rock-solid"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 518.24,
      "durationSeconds": 5.6,
      "text": "foundation. The difference now?"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 520.76,
      "durationSeconds": 6.32,
      "text": "You understand every single line."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 523.84,
      "durationSeconds": 4.76,
      "text": "No more blind copy-paste. Finally, let's"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 527.08,
      "durationSeconds": 5.48,
      "text": "prove it works."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 528.6,
      "durationSeconds": 6.64,
      "text": "Run npx tsc with the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 532.56,
      "durationSeconds": 5.32,
      "text": "no emit flag to type check your whole"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 535.24,
      "durationSeconds": 5.56,
      "text": "project without producing any files."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 537.88,
      "durationSeconds": 5.16,
      "text": "If you see no errors, your config and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 540.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.039,
      "text": "your code are in great shape."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 543.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4,
      "text": "This is the exact command you'd run in a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 544.839,
      "durationSeconds": 4.081,
      "text": "CI pipeline to catch bugs before they"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 547.44,
      "durationSeconds": 3.48,
      "text": "ever reach users."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 548.92,
      "durationSeconds": 6.4,
      "text": "And that's the whole point of mastering"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 550.92,
      "durationSeconds": 6.04,
      "text": "this file. And that's tsconfig.json"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 555.32,
      "durationSeconds": 4.44,
      "text": "fully decoded."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 556.96,
      "durationSeconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Remember the three big takeaways. Always"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 559.76,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "turn on strict mode to catch bugs before"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 562.12,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4,
      "text": "your users do."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 563.6,
      "durationSeconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Use path aliases to kill those ugly"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 566.52,
      "durationSeconds": 4.24,
      "text": "relative imports."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 568.12,
      "durationSeconds": 5.04,
      "text": "And set your target and module to match"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 570.76,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "where your code actually runs."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 573.16,
      "durationSeconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Next up in our TypeScript track, we're"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 575.64,
      "durationSeconds": 6.4,
      "text": "diving into TypeScript generics."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 579,
      "durationSeconds": 4.76,
      "text": "The feature that unlocks truly reusable,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 582.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4.84,
      "text": "type-safe code."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 583.76,
      "durationSeconds": 5.12,
      "text": "If this made TSConfig finally click, hit"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 586.88,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "subscribe and drop your biggest"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 588.88,
      "durationSeconds": 5.48,
      "text": "TypeScript question in the comments."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 591.04,
      "durationSeconds": 3.32,
      "text": "We read every one."
    }
